            <div xml:id="d442">

                <pb facs="0517" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-21T14:00:00+08:00">February 21, 1932—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 21—8:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>94. Referring to my telegram No. 90, February 20, 6 p.m., paragraph 3, regarding
                    protest by Senior Consul on February 20th against use by Japanese forces of
                    International Settlement as a base or channel of military operations. This
                    action by consular body was proposed by French Consul General as a result of my
                    conversations with him under Department’s 22, February 13, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>Not repeated to the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
